{
  "engine_key": "hamilton_ventocr",
  "display_name": "Hamilton",
  "developer": "VentOCR Developer Team",
  "version": "0.2.5",
  "engine_api": 3,
  "ventocr_min": "0.6.2",
  "description": "Hamilton ventilator OCR engine. Breath = display update of Compliance / VTE. OCR (selectable): VTE, Compliance, Ppeak, MinVol, P0.1, mode, set rate / ΔPinsp / PEEP / oxygen. Waveforms: Paw (Pressure), Flow, Volume, and the 4th panel as Pes or Ptranspulm (option post_ocr.ptranspulm) with wrap-around sweep (50 px/s, 22 s per sweep on 1920x1080). Trigger: A (patient-triggered, pink triangle under the Paw time axis) / C (machine-triggered) / blank (unknown: the Paw panel was hidden or covered by a settings dialog, or the screen was cleared during the breath); a new triangle without a display update also starts a breath.",
  "base_resolution": "1920x1080",
  "supported_resolutions": [
    "1920x1080"
  ],
  "has_extract_waves": true,
  "output_columns": {
